{
  "name": "humanoid",
  "description": "Full 26-part humanoid/character body (feet, lower/upper legs with knee joints, hips, torso, shoulders, upper/forearms with elbow joints, hands, neck, head, eyes, optional chest emblem). Same exact numbers as the HUMAN worked recipe in agent/prompts.py - this file is now the single source of truth, prompts.py should stay in sync with it but this JSON is what template.build actually reads. Optional face detail (nose, eyebrows, ears, mouth, and two boolean-cut cheek dimples) is included and controlled by include_optional_parts, same flag as the chest emblem. Note: this is stylized/toy-level facial detail via primitive shapes and one boolean cut per dimple - NOT organic sculpted detail (real skin-fold dimples need Sculpt Mode, which this tool cannot do).",
